     "text": "Okay, I have to tell you about my first Bucs tailgate, because it was the most American thing I’ve ever done.\n\nWe got to the stadium at 10 a.m. The game started at 4:25. Six hours early! I thought my coworker Dave was joking, but the parking lot was already full of trucks, tents, grills and huge speakers playing country music. Everyone was wearing red. Even the dogs had Bucs jerseys.\n\nDave’s group had a whole setup: two grills, three coolers, a TV powered by a generator, and a game called cornhole, where you throw little bags at a wooden board with a hole. I was terrible at it. A man I didn’t know high-fived me anyway and gave me a bratwurst. People were so friendly. Total strangers asked me where I was from, and when I said France, one guy shouted, “Welcome to America! Let’s go Bucs!”\n\nThe game itself was a nail-biter. We were down by four points with one minute left, and then our quarterback threw a perfect pass for a touchdown. The whole stadium exploded. I screamed so loud I lost my voice. I still don’t understand all the rules, but I understand the feeling.\n\nWe got home at 9 p.m., sunburned and exhausted. Would I do it again? Absolutely. Next time I’m bringing a quiche to the tailgate. Somebody has to represent France.",
