       "en": "If you want to avoid gossip politely, you have nice phrases: **“Honestly, I’d rather stay out of it.”**, **“I don’t really know the whole story.”**, **“That’s between them.”**. And if someone tells you a secret: **“Don’t worry, I’ll keep it to myself.”** Being the person who doesn’t spread rumors makes people trust you, and trust matters a lot in American workplaces.",
       "fr": "Si tu veux éviter les potins poliment, tu as de bonnes phrases : « Honestly, I’d rather stay out of it. », « I don’t really know the whole story. », « That’s between them. ». Et si quelqu’un te confie un secret : « Don’t worry, I’ll keep it to myself. ». Être la personne qui ne répand pas les rumeurs donne confiance aux gens, et la confiance compte beaucoup dans le monde du travail américain.",
