     "text": "On Monday morning, Brianna at the front desk mentioned to Marcus that Dr. Patel was “thinking about changing some things in the office.” She meant the waiting room chairs. They’re old, and patients complain about them.\n\nMarcus told Jake that Dr. Patel was planning big changes. Jake told Lisa, the office manager, that he’d heard the office might be reorganized. By lunchtime, Kim from billing was telling everyone in the break room that apparently, someone was going to be let go. Supposedly, it was going to be someone from the hygiene team.\n\nClaire heard the rumor at 2 p.m. Marcus looked worried. “I heard it through the grapevine,” he said. “Apparently, they’re cutting a hygienist position.” Claire was new. She was sure it was her. She spent the whole afternoon feeling sick.\n\nAt 5 p.m., Dr. Patel walked into the break room with a catalog. “Okay, team, I need your opinions. Which chairs do you like better, the blue ones or the gray ones?”\n\nEveryone stared at her. Then Brianna started laughing. “Wait. That’s what you were talking about? The chairs?”\n\n“Of course,” said Dr. Patel. “What did you think I meant?”\n\nNobody answered. Later, Claire told her husband the whole story. “The lesson,” she said, “is that if you hear a rumor, ask the source.” Tom laughed. “Or just stay out of it.” For the record, the team chose the blue chairs.",
