       "en": "**The Fourth of July** (Independence Day) celebrates 1776, when the US declared independence from Britain. It’s a summer party: barbecues, flags, red-white-and-blue everything, and **fireworks** at night. In Tampa, people watch fireworks over the bay downtown. **Halloween** (October 31st) is huge too: kids wear **costumes** and go **trick-or-treating** from door to door. Adults have costume parties. Buy candy, or you’ll be the house with no candy!",
